help visualize how policies would work out. The actual UI/UX might differ.<=
/span></p>
    <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"468" style=3D"width:641=
px;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"2a5c9878cd9a0e212b5e9b7780cc184b1946d7c73478fed=
e3f432439224f2c41" height=3D"1220"></p>
   </div>
  </div>
  <p><br></p>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"rwui_tab_content" data-name=3D"Access Control" data-hash=3D"=
tab-Access+Control">
  <p><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;"><strong>N.B.</strong> Move to the next =
pages on the diagram to see the CX &amp; IIS access control solution detail=
s</span></p>
  <p><img class=3D"drawio-diagram-image" width=3D"468" style=3D"width:746px=
;max-width: 100%;" src=3D"de1663d1e743298e8da182c3932f7a5cbfc08ad8e21337931=
1c82c77718649c4" height=3D"326"></p>
  <p>Ref.&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://developer.okta.co=
m/docs/concepts/inline-hooks/" rel=3D"nofollow">https://developer.okta.com/=
docs/concepts/inline-hooks/</a></p>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"rwui_tab_content" data-name=3D"Functional Requirements" data=
-hash=3D"tab-Functional+Requirements">
  <div class=3D"table-wrap">
   <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" style=3D"width: =
81.7954%;">
    <colgroup class=3D"">
     <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 6.32238%;">
     <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 8.10692%;">
     <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 44.6645%;">
     <col class=3D"" style=3D"width: 40.8892%;">
    </colgroup>
    <tbody class=3D"">
     <tr class=3D"">
      <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Req. No.</th>
      <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Category</th>
      <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Description</th>
      <th class=3D"confluenceTh">Comments</th>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.ST.001</td>
      <td rowspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p>Storage</p>
       </div>
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p>In the policy store, files should be organized and named as foll=
ow:</p>
        <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
         <div class=3D"codeHeader panelHeader pdl" style=3D"border-bottom-w=
idth: 1px;">
          <b>Folder structure &amp; naming convention</b>
         </div>
         <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
          <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-param=
s=3D"brush: java; gutter: false">&lt;userid&gt;/&lt;userid&gt;-&lt;config&g=
t;.json</pre>
         </div>
        </div>
        <p>Where:</p>
        <ul>
         <li data-uuid=3D"22497c71-9c33-4d69-abed-d0ad2da8c86a">&lt;userId&=
gt; =3D login user id</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"f8a400a2-01a4-44ec-b0af-b98feb87bb70">&lt;config&=
gt; =3D [identity, features, data,&nbsp;<span style=3D"color:#09326c;">syst=
em</span>, preferences]=20
          <ul>
           <li><em>Identity</em> is for identity profile</li>
           <li><em>Feature</em>&nbsp;is for application feature access poli=
cies</li>
           <li><em>Data</em> is for sales-structured data access policies</=
li>
           <li><em>System</em> is for system settings</li>
           <li><em>Preferences</em> is for application preferences</li>
          </ul></li>
        </ul>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p>Concerns:</p>
        <ul>
         <li data-uuid=3D"ac4f85c8-1d6f-467d-84c2-6361b069c73e">Conflicting=
&nbsp; user id (i.e. config folder, config file name, user id itself)</li>
        </ul>
       </div></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.ST.002</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>S3 Versioning</strong> feature should be enabled upfront=
 in preparation for access management versioning functionality</p>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><br></p>
       </div></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.PR.001</td>
      <td rowspan=3D"7" class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p>Provisioning</p>
       </div>
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
       </div>
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
       </div>
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
       </div>
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
       </div>
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
       </div>
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>Application feature access policies</strong>&nbsp;must f=
ollow the following schema:</p>
        <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
         <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
          <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-param=
s=3D"brush: xml; gutter: true">{
=09"statement": [
=09=09{
=09=09 &nbsp; &nbsp;"id": "",
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; "effect": "",
=09=09=09"principal": "",
=09=09=09"org":"",
=09=09=09"package": [""],
=09=09=09"resource": [""],
=09=09=09"action": [""],
=09=09=09"condition": [""]
        }
    ]
}</pre>
         </div>
        </div>
        <p>Where:</p>
        <ul>
         <li data-uuid=3D"c8c6bbb0-2458-473a-ae95-fe77e3c0c2d9"><em>id</em>=
 is the statement policy identifier</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"d3b4764d-ba40-4d93-b844-5dc04c729c6c"><em>effect<=
/em> =3D [allow, deny]</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"85385013-a35f-40b4-b896-4000e9f31587"><em>princip=
al</em> =3D &lt;type&gt;:[&lt;userId&gt;, &lt;firmId&gt;]=20
          <ul>
           <li>&lt;type&gt; =3D [user, firm]</li>
          </ul></li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"f8844a8e-69f1-4cd2-81cc-47d71e0a6401"><em>org</em=
> =3D &lt;firmId&gt;:*</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"58e693aa-13ea-4aec-88f6-bec7dcfce1db"><em>package=
</em> is the list of assigned packages, e.g. &lt;packageName&gt;:*</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"2d02d3a6-b6e7-4342-801a-0255f4b2bb24"><em>resourc=
e</em> is the list of additional (allowed/denied) resources, e.g. &lt;modul=
eName&gt;:&lt;capabilityName&gt;:::&lt;resourceName&gt;</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"1d8a8214-2128-4b31-97fc-b3472148fbec"><em>action<=
/em> is the list of (allowed/denied) permissions, e.g. &lt;moduleName&gt;:&=
lt;capabilityName&gt;:::&lt;permissionName&gt;</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"6946a28c-b2cb-498a-8af3-a38a2c8e90a9"><em>conditi=
on</em> is a list of rules to apply, taking into account object attributes<=
/li>
        </ul>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><br></p>
       </div></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.PR.002</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>Sales-structured data access</strong> (aka RR Codes)</p>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">TBD</span></p>
       </div></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.PR.003</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>Identity profile configs</strong> must follow the follow=
ing schema:<strong><br></strong></p>
        <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
         <div class=3D"codeHeader panelHeader pdl" style=3D"border-bottom-w=
idth: 1px;">
          <b>HTTP Request Body</b>
         </div>
         <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
          <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-param=
s=3D"brush: xml; gutter: true">{
=09"firmId": "",
&nbsp; &nbsp; "username": "",
=09"firstName": "",
=09"lastName": "",
=09"email": ""
}</pre>
         </div>
        </div>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><br></p>
       </div></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.PR.004</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>Application preferences</strong> must follow the followi=
ng schema:</p>
        <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
         <div class=3D"codeHeader panelHeader pdl" style=3D"border-bottom-w=
idth: 1px;">
          <b>HTTP Request Body</b>
         </div>
         <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
          <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-param=
s=3D"brush: xml; gutter: true">{
=09"preferredLanguage": ""
}</pre>
         </div>
        </div>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><br></p>
       </div></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.PR.005</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>System settings</strong> must follow the following schem=
a:</p>
        <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
         <div class=3D"codeHeader panelHeader pdl" style=3D"border-bottom-w=
idth: 1px;">
          <b>HTTP Request Body</b>
         </div>
         <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
          <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-param=
s=3D"brush: xml; gutter: true">{
=09"cx": {
=09=09"roleScopeType": "",
=09=09"userGroup": "",
=09=09"isFirmScope": "",
=09=09"userRole": "",
  &nbsp; =09"idp": ""
=09},=20

&nbsp; &nbsp; "r2": {
=09=09"compassR2Id": ""
=09},

=09"sz": {
=09=09"secureZoneIds": [""]
=09},

=09"oss": {
=09=09"ossId": "",
=09=09"ossProxyId": "", //deprecated
=09=09"ossUserId": "", //deprecated=20
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; "ossGroupId": "" //deprecated=20
&nbsp; &nbsp; },

=09"okta": { //deprecated. Should be provided dynamically by Okta
=09 &nbsp; &nbsp;"idpUserId": "",
=09 &nbsp; &nbsp;"idpSubject": "",
=09&nbsp; &nbsp; "sourceIdpSubject": "",
=09=09"externalClientId": "",
=09=09"bngfReferenceId": ""
=09}
}</pre>
         </div>
        </div>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><br></p>
       </div></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.PR.006</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>Provisioning requests</strong> must follow the following=
 schema:</p>
        <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
         <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
          <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-param=
s=3D"brush: xml; gutter: true">{
=09"requests": [{
=09=09"id": "",
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; "action": "",
=09=09"source": ""
&nbsp; &nbsp; }]
}</pre>
         </div>
        </div>
        <p>Where:</p>
        <ul>
         <li data-uuid=3D"b4de945a-8986-4118-8038-bbe213206e01"><em>id</em>=
 is the request identifier</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"f30115ae-9f23-4b8c-b6eb-1c47a25e774a"><em>action<=
/em>&nbsp;=3D [create, update, delete]</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"d0ef47a0-c42d-49ee-ac5c-a6626c4c9e2a"><em>source<=
/em> is the&nbsp;location of the config/policy file in the case of a create=
/update action</li>
        </ul>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><br></p>
       </div></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.PR.007</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
        <p><strong>Provisioning responses </strong>must follow the followin=
g schema:</p>
        <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
         <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
          <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-param=
s=3D"brush: xml; gutter: true">{
=09"response": [{
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; "requestId": "",
=09=09"status": "",
=09=09"message": ""
&nbsp; &nbsp; }]
}</pre>
         </div>
        </div>
        <p>Where:</p>
        <ul>
         <li data-uuid=3D"ed9c3e7e-3e0b-45d7-9f7d-f24a95d05083"><em>request=
Id</em> is the original request identifier&nbsp;</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"a1eb7cf4-c904-49ff-b0cb-eaa943a78894"><em>status<=
/em> =3D [pending, completed, failed]</li>
         <li data-uuid=3D"add4ff4f-57d4-4908-912c-94ce23b621fd"><em>message=
</em> is the detailed status message (optional)</li>
        </ul>
       </div></td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.OP.001</td>
      <td rowspan=3D"4" class=3D"confluenceTd">System settings</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Username</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <p>Optional (i.e. If not entered manually, will be generated.)</p>
       <ul>
        <li data-uuid=3D"5c44a1a9-7130-46bd-8928-e3ef9389bd3d">Manual-entry=
 to be validated=20
         <ul>
          <li>Currently, <strong>local users</strong> have their <em>userna=
me</em> manually entered and validated (N.B. No dependency on Okta)</li>
          <li>Delayed provisioning should render a different one if the ent=
ered <em>username</em> ends up being taken in the meantime.=20
           <ul>
            <li>Must be emailed out</li>
            <li>Should allow <em>username</em> to be modified afterward</li=
>
           </ul></li>
         </ul></li>
        <li data-uuid=3D"7c0ccf79-3082-47ce-8691-2811f0901293">System-gener=
ated=20
         <ul>
          <li>Must be emailed out</li>
          <li>Currently, the <em>username</em> for <strong>SSO users</stron=
g> is a copy of <em>IDP Subject</em> (Okta) which itself is a copy of <em>B=
NGF Reference ID</em> (Okta) which is a combination of <em>BNGF Identity So=
urce</em> (Okta) and the <em>SSO username</em> (3rd party IDP)</li>
          <li>Similarly, the <em>username</em> for <strong>NBC employees</s=
trong> must be a copy of <em>IDP Subject</em> (Okta) which itself is a copy=
 of <em>BNGF Reference ID</em> (Okta) which would be the employee's <em>sho=
rt ID</em> (IIQ)</li>
         </ul></li>
       </ul></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.OP.002</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">SZ IDs</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <ul>
        <li data-uuid=3D"d1518334-f040-4fc6-96c6-5d325c383401">Must have be=
en created in advance</li>
       </ul></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.OP.003</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">R2 ID</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <ul>
        <li data-uuid=3D"e3d40655-0a9f-4c8c-b91f-eb81ade4aa53">Must have be=
en created in advance</li>
       </ul></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.OP.004</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">OSS ID</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <ul>
        <li data-uuid=3D"c7d1e72f-bdaa-4d74-87b4-dcb23eeca68e">Must have be=
en created in advance</li>
       </ul></td>
     </tr>
     <tr class=3D"">
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FR.OP.005</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Offboarding</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">:question:&nbsp;</td>
      <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
       <ul>
        <li data-uuid=3D"4cfeaf10-a264-4a79-8b07-ac87d7993bcf">Should it pa=
ss by the provisioning process?</li>
        <li data-uuid=3D"458d57d5-1f5f-442e-bdf6-896ffd85606e">How should i=
t work in the future when only the identity will reside in the database and=
 the access profiles will be in the object store</li>
       </ul></td>
     </tr>
    </tbody>
   </table>
  </div>
  <p><br></p>
 </div>
